          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most basements, the Frigidaire 50-pint on a hose to a floor drain is all you need: Energy Star efficient, simple to live with, and big enough for most basements under roughly 1,500 square feet. If the drain is uphill, buy the GE pump model. If you must use a bucket, the Midea Cube stretches the time between trips. If the basement is large, cold, or chronically damp, skip the portables and go straight to the Aprilaire E080 or a Santa Fe unit.
          </p>
